WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:18.464
Marilla put her knitting on her lap. Her eyes were tired again.

2
00:00:18.465 --> 00:00:24.227
Anne was curled up on the rug in front of the fire. Marilla looked at her with tenderness.

3
00:00:24.228 --> 00:00:27.719
Anne had no idea of how much Marilla loved her.

4
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.052
Anne sometimes thought Marilla was hard to please and lacked understanding.

5
00:00:32.053 --> 00:00:36.866
But she always stopped that thought and remembered what she owed to Marilla.

6
00:00:36.867 --> 00:00:41.734
"Anne," Marilla said abruptly, "Miss Stacy was here this afternoon."

7
00:00:41.735 --> 00:00:44.802
"Was she? Why?" asked Anne.

8
00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:48.037
"She came to talk about you," answered Marilla.

9
00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:55.125
"About me?" Anne looked rather scared. Then she flushed and exclaimed, "Oh, I know what she said.

10
00:00:55.126 --> 00:00:59.458
I meant to tell you, Marilla, honestly I did, but I forgot.

11
00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:06.671
Miss Stacy caught me reading Ben-Hur in school when I should have been studying Canadian history.

12
00:01:06.672 --> 00:01:11.092
"I was reading it at lunch and was at the chariot race when lunch ended.

13
00:01:11.093 --> 00:01:13.734
I was dying to know what happened.

14
00:01:13.735 --> 00:01:18.010
So I opened my history book and put Ben-Hur on my lap.

15
00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:20.448
It looked like I was studying history.

16
00:01:20.449 --> 00:01:25.995
I was so interested in it that I never noticed Miss Stacy looking down at me.

17
00:01:25.996 --> 00:01:32.174
I was very ashamed, Marilla, especially when I heard Josie Pye giggling."

18
00:01:32.175 --> 00:01:39.651
Marilla listened with a frown. "Miss Stacy didn't mention that, Anne. It's just your guilty conscience.

19
00:01:39.652 --> 00:01:46.118
Miss Stacy wants to organize a class of students to study for the entrance exam of Queen's College.

20
00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:49.782
She asked Matthew and me if we would like you to join it.

21
00:01:49.783 --> 00:01:53.761
Would you like to go to Queen's College and become a teacher, Anne?"

22
00:01:53.762 --> 00:01:56.891
"Oh, Marilla!" Anne got up from the rug.

23
00:01:56.892 --> 00:02:01.215
"I'd love to be a teacher, but isn't it expensive?"

24
00:02:01.216 --> 00:02:08.122
"Don't worry about that," Marilla said. "Education is important, for girls as much as boys."

25
00:02:08.123 --> 00:02:16.687
"Oh, thank you, Marilla! I'll study as hard as I can, though I warn you not to expect much in geometry," Anne said.

26
00:02:16.688 --> 00:02:25.339
The Queen's class was organized. Gilbert Blythe, Anne Shirley, Ruby Gillis, Josie Pye, and Charlie Sloane joined.

27
00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:30.911
Diana Barry did not, as her parents did not intend to send her to Queen's College.

28
00:02:30.912 --> 00:02:35.602
It was the first time that Diana and Anne had been separated in anything.

29
00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:42.339
When the Queen's class stayed after school for extra lessons, Anne saw Diana leave slowly with the others.

30
00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:48.313
A lump came into Anne's throat, and she hid behind her Latin book to hide the tears in her eyes.

31
00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:53.234
She would never let Gilbert Blythe or Josie Pye see those tears.

32
00:02:53.235 --> 00:02:56.196
Anne enjoyed the Queen's class very much.

33
00:02:56.197 --> 00:03:00.864
She chatted away to Marilla, "Jane and Ruby are studying to be teachers.

34
00:03:00.865 --> 00:03:04.693
Ruby says she'll study for two years and then get married.

35
00:03:04.694 --> 00:03:11.411
Jane says she'll never marry because you are paid for teaching, but a husband won't pay you anything."

36
00:03:11.412 --> 00:03:15.219
"What is Gilbert Blythe going to be?" asked Marilla.

37
00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.964
"I don't know what Gilbert's ambition is—if he has one," said Anne scornfully.

38
00:03:20.965 --> 00:03:28.316
Since the day Gilbert had rescued Anne from the bridge and she had not forgiven him, Gilbert had steadily ignored Anne.

39
00:03:28.317 --> 00:03:32.788
He talked and joked with the other girls and sometimes walked them home.

40
00:03:32.789 --> 00:03:38.605
But he simply ignored Anne, and Anne found that it was not pleasant to be ignored.

41
00:03:38.606 --> 00:03:44.453
Mrs. Lynde came to Green Gables one afternoon to find out why Marilla had not come to visit her.

42
00:03:44.454 --> 00:03:49.590
"Matthew had chest pains," Marilla explained, "and I thought I shouldn't leave him.

43
00:03:49.591 --> 00:03:54.028
He's all right now, but he gets chest pains more often.

44
00:03:54.029 --> 00:03:57.050
Sit down, Rachel. Will you stay for tea?"

45
00:03:57.051 --> 00:04:00.605
Mrs. Lynde and Marilla ate some biscuits Anne had made.

46
00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.689
Mrs. Lynde thought the biscuits were delicious.

47
00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:11.359
"Anne has turned out to be a real smart girl," admitted Mrs. Lynde. "She must be a great help."

48
00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:16.256
"She is," said Marilla, "and she's steady and reliable too.

49
00:04:16.257 --> 00:04:22.764
I was afraid she'd never stop her daydreaming, but she has. I trust her with anything now."

50
00:04:22.765 --> 00:04:32.583
Mrs. Lynde continued, "Yes, she really improved these three years, especially in looks. You could even say she's pretty."

51
00:04:32.584 --> 00:04:40.985
Anne enjoyed her vacation thoroughly. She and Diana spent most of the time outdoors, walking, rowing, and wandering.

52
00:04:40.986 --> 00:04:46.141
When September came, she was ready to study. The Queen's exam loomed.

53
00:04:46.142 --> 00:04:50.671
Anne had a nightmare where she was staring at the pass list for the exam.

54
00:04:50.672 --> 00:04:55.057
Gilbert's name was on top and her name was absent.

55
00:04:55.058 --> 00:05:01.728
The school year passed quickly. Soon June came and the Queen's exams were held in Charlottetown.

56
00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:06.157
"Dearest Diana," wrote Anne in a letter back home to her friend.

57
00:05:06.158 --> 00:05:11.231
"Today we had the history and geometry exam. Geometry was hard.

58
00:05:11.232 --> 00:05:16.459
Josie Pye said the geometry was so easy, a ten-year-old could have done it.

59
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.914
Oh Diana, I wish you were here with me!"

60
00:05:19.915 --> 00:05:25.086
Anne returned to Avonlea and waited for the results to be published in the newspaper.

61
00:05:25.087 --> 00:05:30.588
While she wanted to beat Gilbert Blythe, she also wanted to do well for Matthew and Marilla—

62
00:05:30.589 --> 00:05:34.442
especially Matthew, who said she "would beat the whole island."

63
00:05:34.443 --> 00:05:37.369
That would only happen in her wildest dreams!

64
00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.802
But she hoped she would be among the top ten students.

65
00:05:40.803 --> 00:05:46.182
Finally Anne saw Diana racing to Green Gables with a newspaper in her hand.

66
00:05:46.183 --> 00:05:51.625
Anne sprang to her feet. The pass list had been printed! Anne's head whirled.

67
00:05:51.626 --> 00:06:00.766
"Anne, you've passed!" Diana cried. "Passed first—you and Gilbert both. You've tied! Oh, I'm so proud."

68
00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:04.443
Anne grabbed the paper. Yes, she had passed.

69
00:06:04.444 --> 00:06:08.291
There was her name at the very top of a list of two hundred!

70
00:06:08.292 --> 00:06:13.478
That moment was worth living for. Everyone from Avonlea had passed!

71
00:06:13.479 --> 00:06:15.932
They hurried to tell Matthew and Marilla.

72
00:06:15.933 --> 00:06:25.325
"Oh, Matthew," exclaimed Anne, "I've passed and I'm first—or one of the first. I'm not vain, but I'm thankful."

73
00:06:25.326 --> 00:06:30.129
"Well now, I've always said it," said Matthew, gazing at the list happily.

74
00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.360
"I knew you could beat them all."

75
00:06:32.361 --> 00:06:47.988
"You've done pretty well, I must say, Anne," said Marilla, trying to hide her extreme pride. "We're all proud of you."
